<p>Russia and Ukraine accused each other of violating a 32-hour Orthodox Easter ceasefire that began on Saturday and expired at the end of Sunday. Both sides reported large numbers of attacks during the pause. The truce offered a brief opening for reduced violence during one of the most important holidays in the Orthodox calendar, and several reports noted at least some lull in Russian air raids even as claims of shelling, drone strikes, and ground assaults continued. Ukraine’s military said it recorded 2,299 alleged Russian violations, including 28 assault actions, 479 shellings, 747 attack-drone strikes, and 1,045 FPV-drone strikes, while Russia’s Defence Ministry accused Kyiv of nearly 2,000 breaches. After the ceasefire ended, a Donetsk regional official in Ukraine said Russian troops killed two people and injured one before the pause expired, underscoring how little humanitarian relief the truce delivered.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/p3fUtpY8zk3ap8s-DXZ_9slZQkulakDzt77JQ8Uuj5RGV79T95IhpOxV4xQncVQE11Zd2UCdWj4QAMTZJJ0ENMviYRoeU8tIgadrcSmukKuG4rhvy-SqAgtHyw_ur0bfDnjsxIJVDWUuTgh3Ijh1oYH3FhRIADO6n0-fyWXNpuxntk0zw3VdpzMNjkLWTo_f3OshLv29uFUMGm1gCHpLGcLD_jQVmMSw3gczhWdVvR_2v9643T_E0NnRJYb5h1HiM6ORexQ0h5vdamgwVAg-7JNfk0gNYPKBDezHqqHUujx_v8PR_Xyxv3L-W0pyEFa6b3oARF_4leX4lkdeZXzWv5RnQCrwZBDR8Bbb4i8dMdQCUVcWi048qwPvEDD7fipHRSXeDT6UxpVDyAoA-9vheYwscF0_balRVIKIxvsftNTtdVcf3nDRUl7IbeWdrMiKG_AFVxXzg47uTEWjP93Do3GFraz_d5nZkgE1vyxKamOGVHsW' alt='Scene linked to coverage of the Orthodox Easter ceasefire between Russia and Ukraine.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Competing claims over who initiated the idea: SCMP said Zelensky had proposed a pause more than a week earlier, before Putin announced the Easter ceasefire on Thursday.</li><li>Documentation gap: Ukraine released a category-by-category accounting of alleged violations, while Russia’s public accusation in these reports appeared mainly as an overall total.</li><li>Declared versus enforced: Reports said both sides agreed to observe the truce, but accusations of breaches surfaced soon after it began.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ukrainian military: Kyiv emphasized that drone strikes, along with shelling and assaults, were still being reported during the Easter pause. (<a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/ukraine-russia-accuse-each-other-of-easter-truce-violations/article70854753.ece'>The Hindu</a>)</li><li>Russian Defence Ministry: Moscow said Ukrainian forces had not observed the Easter truce and argued that Kyiv was responsible for breaking it. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/easter-truce-between-ukraine-and-russia-ends'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Volodymyr Zelensky: Coverage showed Zelensky marking Easter while pairing his holiday message with accusations that Russian attacks continued. (<a href='https://www.dw.com/en/zelenskyy-putin-mark-easter-amid-truce-breach-allegations/a-76754232'>DW</a>)</li><li>Vladimir Putin: Reports said Putin cast the pause as an Easter-linked measure tied to Orthodox observance. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/europe/article/3349820/russia-and-ukraine-accuse-each-other-violating-putins-easter-ceasefire'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-russia-and-ukraine-trade-blame-after-orthodox-easter-truce-violations/'>Russia and Ukraine trade blame after Orthodox Easter truce violations</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://abcnews.com/International/wireStory/russia-ukraine-accuse-violating-orthodox-easter-ceasefire-131966392'>Russia and Ukraine accuse each other of violating Orthodox Easter ceasefire</a> - abcnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/two-killed-in-ukraine-despite-easter-ceasefire-governor-says'>Two killed in Ukraine despite Easter ceasefire, governor says</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.pbs.org/newshour/world/russia-and-ukraine-accuse-